#
# Main analytical components:
#   1. Data loading and metadata annotation
#   2. Dataset merging and batch correction (Harmony)
#   3. Clustering and cell type annotation
#   4. ASPC subpopulation re-clustering
#   5. Differential expression analysis (Diet-specific comparisons)
#   6. Persistent HFD-responsive gene identification
#   7. Functional enrichment (GO, KEGG, Reactome, GSEA)
#   8. Expression heatmaps and proportion analysis
#
# Software environment:
#   R version >= 4.2
#   Seurat v4
#   Harmony
#   clusterProfiler
#   org.Mm.eg.db
#
# Notes:
#   - Gene annotations are based on mouse genome (org.Mm.eg.db).
#   - Batch effects corrected using Harmony (grouped by Depot and Diet).
#   - Differential expression filtering threshold:
#       min.pct = 0.25, logfc.threshold = 0.25, p_val_adj < 0.05
#
